tting the result back (this system → n8n)**\n   - Once a run finishes, `notifyWebhook()` fires a one-shot `POST` to `WEBHOOK_URL` (if set) with `{ runId, agentKey, status, summary, costUsd, linearTasks }`.\n   - It's fire-and-forget — if the webhook receiver is down, it just logs an error and doesn't affect the run itself (which already completed).\n   - Alternative to polling: n8n could instead poll `GET /api/runs/:id` for status, or use `GET /api/runs/:id/stream` (SSE) for live events, but the webhook is the \"no polling needed\" path.\n\nSo a typical n8n workflow would be: **HTTP Request node** → `POST /api/automation/runs` with the API key → **Webhook node** (its URL set as `WEBHOOK_URL` on this server) to receive the finished result asynchronously.\n\nNote: I didn't find `AUTOMATION_API_KEY` or `WEBHOOK_URL` set anywhere (no `.env.example` in the repo) — so this wiring exists in code but isn't currently configured/active. If you want it live, someone needs to set those two env vars on the server.","linearTasks":[],"archived":false},{"id":"bfa52f5b-347e-49bb-a23a-fca88ea9a632","goal":"test run from n8n","agentKey":"sales","status":"success","createdAt":"2026-08-07T07:12:53.575Z","finishedAt":"2026-08-07T07:13:03.277Z","costUsd":0.023760999999999997,"summary":"This looks like a connectivity/test trigger from n8n rather than an actual task — no specific deliverable was requested (no target prospect, campaign, or content brief included).\n\nI haven't taken any action (no documents created, no emails drafted, nothing posted) since there's nothing to act on yet.\n\nTo produce something useful, let me know things like:\n- **Outreach email/sequence**: target customer segment, product/offer, pricing, key differentiators, and the prospect's name/email\n- **Proposal draft**: client name, scope, pricing structure\n- **Social post/DM**: platform, topic/angle, and which connected account to use (I can run `list_zernio_accounts` to check what's linked)\n- **Pipeline plan**: current stage definitions or goals for the quarter\n\nSend over a real task (or confirm this was just a connectivity check) and I'll generate the actual draft.","linearTasks":[],"archived":false},{"id":"3f85a601-9be8-46d0-8db2-c2cb5ddbbeee","goal":"hi, what are the tasks u can do for me?","agentKey":"ceo","status":"success","createdAt":"2026-08-07T05:10:04.468Z","finishedAt":"2026-08-07T05:10:12.597Z","costUsd":0.157795,"summary":"Hi! I'm the CEO agent — I take a goal or signal and turn it into action by analyzing it and delegating to the right specialist(s). Here's what I can coordinate:\n\n- **Manager** – breaks initiatives into concrete tasks and tracks them in Linear\n- **HR** – onboarding checklists, policies, job descriptions\n- **Developer** – writes/edits code, runs commands in a sandboxed workspace\n- **Analysis** – research and written analytical reports (market research, competitive analysis, etc.)\n- **Sales** – outreach drafts, proposals, pipeline plans, LinkedIn company page posts\n- **Finance** – budgets, expense summaries, financial write-ups\n- **Emails** – reads your inbox, drafts or sends email on your behalf\n\nGive me a goal, a problem, or even a rough idea, and I'll figure out who needs to be involved, brief them, and report back what got done. What do you want to tackle?","linearTasks":[],"archived":false},{"id":"479dcc46-03ef-49c8-aee0-9b8f40964f1e","goal":"send the 222-fnb-analytics report to mail id: fabricmaintainance@gmail.com\nthe file is at CEO AGENT/workspace/222-fnb-analytics.docx","agentKey":"ceo","status":"success","createdAt":"2026-08-06T12:00:42.826Z","finishedAt":"2026-08-06T12:12:40.811Z","costUsd":0.69695715,"summary":"Confirmed sent — message ID `19fd6fd55ef824e7`, verified in the mailbox this time.\n\nYou were right to flag it: the Emails agent had reported success, but a follow-up check against the inbox showed no such email existed — the report was inaccurate. I sent it directly instead and independently verified the send wi